cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use DriftJax for academic research, please cite it using the
  metadata below and the foundational method references listed under
  `references`.
title: "DriftJax: A Differentiable 1-D Drift-Diffusion Solar-Cell Simulator in JAX"
abstract: >-
  DriftJax is a one-dimensional, end-to-end differentiable photovoltaic cell
  simulator based on the drift-diffusion model and the Beer-Lambert law for
  optical absorption, programmed in Python using JAX. Gradients of the power
  conversion efficiency (and any scalar figure of merit) with respect to device
  design parameters are obtained transparently through jax.grad(simulate) via an
  implicit-function-theorem adjoint implemented as a custom_vjp.
